gez(){return"Podcasts AM is a player for public podcast feeds. The episodes themselves stay with their podcasters.\n\nCharts and search come from Apple\u2019s public interfaces: the Apple Podcasts Top Shows RSS feed and the iTunes Search and Lookup API. Browsers may not read the charts feed directly, so amapps.app keeps an unchanged copy of it, updated daily.\n\nEpisodes are read from the podcast\u2019s own RSS feed, whose address comes from that lookup. Audio is played from the address the publisher puts in that feed, unchanged. Some podcasters\u2019 servers do not let browsers read their feed; those shows open only in the app.\n\nFor selected shows, extra content comes from amapps.app: short AI summaries, key points, chapters and show notes. These files are kept with hosting providers (Cloudflare, GitHub Pages).\n\nYour subscriptions and listening positions are stored only in this browser.\n\nAll artwork, titles and descriptions belong to the podcasts and to Apple."},
